# 0089-glm-image-prompt-reuse: image prompts resume from kept prompt states under --parallel, keyed by each
# picture's content (a 62-bit key of its kind, shape and pixels in place of its placeholder tokens), and only the
# pictures past the resume point are encoded again (the tower's rows rank 0 still hands the other ranks). Port of
# Mia's AI Lab's 0054-glm-image-prompt-reuse (by @abhicnv007, MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold
# #11, with Mia's review changes; Apache-2.0), adapted to this series: the int64-array resume comparison this tree
# carries (``_ids_array``) is kept as ``_key_array``, the take-over and shared-prefix comparisons match keys, and the
# spill tier (0088) stores and restores image states by their keyed ids (``_ident``, ``tokens``/``keyed`` in
# cuda/spill.py's entry metadata, which 0088 already shipped), so an evicted or restarted image conversation resumes
# too. The one-stream engine (``--parallel 1``) still resumes no image state; prompts whose pictures carry no content
# keys resume none either. With 0090, a picture's decode is also remembered across turns.
# TF_GLM_RESUME_DEBUG=1 logs every resume decision (the kept states' lengths, windows and keys, and each
# candidate's rejection) on both ranks: for diagnosing exactly this class of prefix question.
